  "query_preview": "outlook for all three locations (36 hours to day 7):\nForecast guidance and pattern recognition all points to at least \nscattered shower potential continuing into next weekend, with a few \nthunderstorms mixed in from time to time. A tropical \ndisturbance/circulation located east of Pohnpei/northeast of Kosrae \nwill not only maintain respectable convergence in the cyclonically- \nenhanced monsoon flow, but there may be a few periods of locally \nincreased shower coverage and intensity.\n\nMarine and surf conditions:\nA west to southwest primary and secondary swell will continue through\nthe weekend at Pohnpei and Kosrae, with a slight backing of swell\ndirection due to the previously-mentioned cyclonic flow in the\nmonsoon environment, will allow for a southwest and south swell\ndirection to continue at Majuro. This swell regime will continue to\nbe augmented by the persistent cross-equatorial flow/swell pattern.\nThe net result is elevated surf concerns will continue the next\nseveral days at Kosrae and Majuro as well. Otherwise, mainly gentle\nto light winds currently, may become light to gentle from time to\ntime, especially for the latter half of next week. Seas of 5 to 7\nfeet are anticipated through the forecast period.",
